1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,141
Azure OpenAI is only one way to bring a model to your site.

2
00:00:05,141 --> 00:00:07,881
This video shows the other providers:

3
00:00:07,881 --> 00:00:12,659
OpenAI and the services that copy its API, Ollama for models that run

4
00:00:12,659 --> 00:00:15,844
on your own machine, and Azure AI Inference.

5
00:00:15,844 --> 00:00:20,750
You add them as connections and deployments, in the same admin screens.

6
00:00:25,350 --> 00:00:32,581
The OpenAI provider connects to OpenAI itself, and to every service that follows its API:

7
00:00:32,581 --> 00:00:38,213
DeepSeek, Google Gemini, Together AI, vLLM, LM Studio and many more.

8
00:00:38,213 --> 00:00:41,790
You only change the endpoint and the key.

9
00:00:42,540 --> 00:00:48,400
Ollama runs open models on your own machine or server, with nothing sent to the cloud.

10
00:00:49,150 --> 00:00:55,882
Azure AI Inference connects to the model endpoints of Azure AI Foundry and to GitHub Models.

11
00:00:55,882 --> 00:00:59,110
Azure AI Services deployments add speech.

12
00:01:03,271 --> 00:01:10,331
Open Artificial Intelligence, Provider Connections, click Add Connection, and click Add on OpenAI.

13
00:01:10,797 --> 00:01:13,572
Enter a Title and a Technical name.

14
00:01:13,572 --> 00:01:16,889
The technical name cannot be changed later.

15
00:01:16,889 --> 00:01:22,777
For a service other than OpenAI, enter its Endpoint, the base address of its API.

16
00:01:23,242 --> 00:01:25,877
Enter the API key of the service.

17
00:01:25,877 --> 00:01:29,254
It is stored securely and never shown again.

18
00:01:29,254 --> 00:01:33,442
Click Save, and the connection is ready for deployments.

19
00:01:37,669 --> 00:01:41,398
An Ollama connection needs only a Title and a Technical name.

20
00:01:41,398 --> 00:01:45,573
The address of the Ollama server, and the models it serves, come from

21
00:01:45,573 --> 00:01:49,359
the configuration of the site, which your technical team sets.

22
00:01:53,535 --> 00:01:59,075
An Azure AI Inference connection asks for the Endpoint of the inference service.

23
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:06,857
Authentication type is Default authentication, API key, or Managed identity, with an optional

24
00:02:06,857 --> 00:02:09,209
Managed identity client ID.

25
00:02:09,209 --> 00:02:12,060
Choose API key, and enter the key.

26
00:02:16,249 --> 00:02:18,629
A connection is not a model.

27
00:02:18,629 --> 00:02:25,209
Open Deployments, click Add Deployment, and each provider you enabled appears as a card:

28
00:02:25,209 --> 00:02:31,369
OpenAI, Ollama, Azure AI Inference, Azure OpenAI and Azure AI Services for speech.

29
00:02:31,820 --> 00:02:32,976
Choose OpenAI.

30
00:02:32,976 --> 00:02:37,426
Enter the Model name that the service expects and a Technical name, and

31
00:02:37,426 --> 00:02:39,911
choose the Connection you just added.

32
00:02:39,911 --> 00:02:44,304
On the Model capabilities card, declare what the model can do, such as

33
00:02:44,304 --> 00:02:45,980
tool calling or vision.

34
00:02:50,180 --> 00:02:55,956
Connections and deployments that come from the configuration of the site show as Read-only.

35
00:02:55,956 --> 00:02:59,350
Change them in the configuration, not in the admin.

36
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:05,442
After you add a deployment, choose it as a default under Settings, Artificial

37
00:03:05,442 --> 00:03:07,760
Intelligence, or on a profile.

38
00:03:08,510 --> 00:03:13,476
Use the OpenAI provider for any service that copies the OpenAI API, and

39
00:03:13,476 --> 00:03:16,120
keep keys with your technical team.

40
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:22,685
Pick the provider that fits, add a connection, then a deployment, and choose

41
00:03:22,685 --> 00:03:24,132
it on your profiles.

42
00:03:24,132 --> 00:03:25,580
Thanks for watching.

